<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Fears that the Democratic party=E2=80=99s =
blue wave in this week=E2=80=99s US midterm elections will sink the AI inve=
stment boom are roiling markets, after heavy losses on Wall Street last nig=
ht.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Asia Pacific markets are a sea of red as i=
nvestors ditch tech stocks after more than $3.2tn was wiped off the US stoc=
k market yesterday.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">South Korea=E2=80=99s Kospi was down 6.51%=
 at the close.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In Taiwan, the benchmark Taiex stock index=
 plunged a record 3,737.67 points in early trading. It closed down 1,791 po=
ints, or 4.6%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Japan=E2=80=99s Nikkei share average has p=
osted its worst week in more than six years.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">For the week, the benchmark was down 9.3%,=
 its worst weekly decline since March 2020 during the Covid pandemic.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Europe has joined the global sell-off.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The FTSE 100 index, which tracks blue-chip=
 shares listed in London, has dropped by 166 points, or more than 1.5%, at =
the start of trading to 10,615 points. Most of the hundred stocks on the in=
dex are down.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The pharmaceuticals company AstraZeneca (-=
2.8%) is the top faller on the FTSE 100.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Other fallers include IAG (-1.5%), which o=
wns British Airways, after it missed profit forecasts and warned this morni=
ng that its annual capacity would be slightly lower than a year earlier.</p=
>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Germany=E2=80=99s Dax index is down 1.5%, =
France=E2=80=99s Cac 40 has dropped by 1.2% at the open, Spain=E2=80=99s Ib=
ex is down 1.1%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">After months of warnings that AI valuation=
s were too high, and that the bubble might burst, US investors dashed to th=
e exits en masse yesterday. The Nasdaq tech index slumped by 5.5%, while th=
e Dow Jones industrial average dropped 1,833.06 points, or 3.44%, and the S=
&amp;P 500 lost 4.36%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Memory chip makers, who had been profiting=
 from the AI boom, led the fallers =E2=80=93 SanDisk slumped 22% and Micron=
 and AMD lost 17% of their value.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The chip company Nvidia led the fallers on=
 the DJIA, down more than 9%.</p>
